OUTPUT INSTRUCTIONS

Produce a single JSON object with exactly these fields:

- "reply": string — your honest, conversational response to the oracle; enumerate the groups
  you produced so the oracle knows what was created
- "operation": string — one of: cluster, merge, focus, cross_filter, exclude
- "concept": string or null — the organising principle you used (e.g. "environmental vs human
  dominance", "decade of release", "visual tone"); set this for cluster and cross_filter;
  for merge/focus/exclude you may omit (null)
- "clusters": array — the complete resulting grouping after this operation; each element is:
    { "label": string, "summary": string, "film_ids": [integer, ...] }
  IMPORTANT: the integers in "film_ids" are the INDEX NUMBERS shown in [brackets] in
  CURRENT FILMS above (1 to {{ films | length }}).  Do NOT use any other numbers.

Rules for "clusters":
1. Every value in film_ids must be an index shown in CURRENT FILMS (integers 1 to {{ films | length }}).
2. Each index may appear in at most one cluster.
3. Every cluster must contain at least one index.
4. Do not invent index numbers outside the 1–{{ films | length }} range.

Write the reply honestly: if the result does not closely match the oracle's request, say so.
